subpath2":22,"slices":23},"Eco-Friendly Packaging Ideas To Use | Evri","Looking for eco-friendly packaging ideas? This guide tells you how to use sustainable packaging materials for shipping parcels and more. Read it, here.","everything-you-need-to-know-about-sustainable-packaging.html\u002F\u002Fwww.evri.com\u002Fguides\u002Feverything-you-need-to-know-about-sustainable-packaging",{"id":12,"type":13,"tags":14,"lang":16,"slug":17,"first_publication_date":18,"last_publication_date":18,"uid":17,"link_type":19,"key":20,"isBroken":21},"ZL-1EREAACAAEkhR","subpath1",[15],"Guides","en-gb","guides","2023-07-25T12:59:36+0000","Document","cf333ebb-0a17-4b76-9935-24bc46a0f081",false,{"link_type":19},[24,55,89,109,148,177,221,250,271],{"variation":25,"version":26,"items":27,"primary":29,"id":53,"slice_type":54,"slice_label":30},"default-slice","sktwi1xtmkfgx8626",[28],{},{"theme":30,"PageHeaderTitle":31,"PageHeaderText":32,"PageHeaderCtaText":30,"PageHeaderCtaUrl":37,"secondaryCtaText":30,"secondaryCtaLabel":30,"secondaryCtaUrl":39,"PageHeaderImage":40,"heroImage":51,"videoContent":52,"showPremiumLogo":30},null,"Everything you need to know about sustainable packaging",[33],{"type":34,"text":35,"spans":36},"paragraph","",[],{"link_type":38},"Any",{"link_type":38},{"dimensions":41,"alt":44,"copyright":30,"url":45,"id":46,"edit":47},{"width":42,"height":43},300,65,"Wrap","everything-you-need-to-know-about-sustainable-packaging.html\u002F\u002Fev-mercury.cdn.prismic.io\u002Fev-mercury\u002Fa76e9a48-a69a-4059-8184-2c60875ba1a4_wrap.svg","YhYpMRIAACkA0QCA",{"x":48,"y":48,"zoom":49,"background":50},0,1,"#fff",{},{"link_type":19},"page_header$9b8cb54f-223f-413e-bffa-e5cd5534bdf9","page_header",{"variation":56,"version":26,"items":57,"primary":59,"id":87,"slice_type":88,"slice_label":30},"cardWithImageNoCta",[58],{},{"CardImage":60,"CardAvatar":70,"CardTitle":71,"CardText":72,"IsEco":21},{"dimensions":61,"alt":64,"copyright":30,"url":65,"id":66,"edit":67},{"width":62,"height":63},1000,665,"An Evri Courier is walking down the street in a residential area with a parcel under his arm.","everything-you-need-to-know-about-sustainable-packaging.html\u002F\u002Fimages.prismic.io\u002Fev-mercury\u002FZ69xb5bqstJ9-pU1_EVRI_LOCATION_01_0782.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&rect=0%2C8%2C8192%2C5448&w=1000&h=665","Z69xb5bqstJ9-pU1",{"x":48,"y":68,"zoom":49,"background":69},8,"transparent","none","Sustainable packaging for sending parcels",[73],{"type":34,"text":74,"spans":75,"direction":86},"Using sustainable packaging when sending parcels is more important than ever, with it being just one part of an overall green shipping initiative. Read on to find out how to wrap a parcel using sustainable packaging, why this can have an impact, and what kind of packaging is considered sustainable.",[76,84],{"start":77,"end":78,"type":79,"data":80},120,134,"hyperlink",{"link_type":81,"url":82,"target":83},"Web","everything-you-need-to-know-about-sustainable-packaging.html\u002F\u002Fwww.evri.com\u002Fguides\u002Fhow-can-your-business-utilise-green-shipping","_self",{"start":77,"end":78,"type":85},"strong","ltr","card$14106682-5729-4eb0-896b-0f463cb270f3","card",{"variation":25,"version":26,"items":90,"primary":92,"id":108,"slice_type":88,"slice_label":30},[91],{},{"CardImage":93,"CardAvatar":70,"CardTitle":99,"CardText":100,"ButtonText":30,"ButtonUrl":107,"IsEco":21},{"dimensions":94,"alt":95,"copyright":30,"url":96,"id":97,"edit":98},{"width":62,"height":63},"An older woman is wrapping a parcel. She is admiring the finished product.","everything-you-need-to-know-about-sustainable-packaging.html\u002F\u002Fimages.prismic.io\u002Fev-mercury\u002FZ6oxO5bqstJ9-cVt_EVRI_LOCATION_06_10405.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&rect=0%2C8%2C7810%2C5194&w=1000&h=665","Z6oxO5bqstJ9-cVt",{"x":48,"y":68,"zoom":49,"background":69},"What is sustainable packaging?",[101,104],{"type":34,"text":102,"spans":103},"Sustainable packaging refers to any packaging that has a lower environmental impact than less sustainable alternatives, such as single-use plastic. ",[],{"type":34,"text":105,"spans":106},"Environmentally friendly packaging and sustainable packaging aren’t always the same. However, the use of sustainable materials when developing these newer, greener packaging alternatives is said to have a positive effect on the environment. ",[],{"link_type":38},"card$e9d8b16b-1a86-42dc-bb6f-66d4bde7727f",{"variation":110,"version":26,"items":111,"primary":143,"id":146,"slice_type":147,"slice_label":30},"listNoIcon",[112,118,123,128,133,138],{"title":30,"content":113,"isNumbered":117},[114],{"type":34,"text":115,"spans":116},"It stops the use of toxic materials that can be used when producing packaging.",[],true,{"title":30,"content":119,"isNumbered":117},[120],{"type":34,"text":121,"spans":122},"It considerably reduces packaging waste.",[],{"title":30,"content":124,"isNumbered":117},[125],{"type":34,"text":126,"spans":127},"It reduces your carbon footprint.",[],{"title":30,"content":129,"isNumbered":117},[130],{"type":34,"text":131,"spans":132},"If you’re a business, using different types of eco-friendly packaging shows your customers that you’re an eco-conscious brand.",[],{"title":30,"content":134,"isNumbered":117},[135],{"type":34,"text":136,"spans":137},"It can lower the price of packaging materials.",[],{"title":30,"content":139,"isNumbered":117},[140],{"type":34,"text":141,"spans":142},"It promotes the use of recyclable and renewable resources.",[],{"theme":30,"title":144,"description":145,"showPaddingTop":21},"What are the benefits of eco-friendly packaging?","There are many advantages to using eco-friendly packaging:","list_block$d9634273-9b34-496e-8d6b-7306e541bd39","list_block",{"variation":25,"version":26,"items":149,"primary":151,"id":175,"slice_type":176,"slice_label":30},[150],{},{"Image":152},{"dimensions":153,"alt":156,"copyright":30,"url":157,"id":158,"edit":159,"tablet":161,"mobile":168},{"width":154,"height":155},1200,280,"ParcelShop store assistant is smiling and using a blue hand-held device to scan multiple parcels placed on the countertop in front of them. The customer can be seen in the foreground.","everything-you-need-to-know-about-sustainable-packaging.html\u002F\u002Fimages.prismic.io\u002Fev-mercury\u002FZ6TI_pbqstJ9-Tfc_EVRI_LOCATION_03_2589.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&rect=0%2C2173%2C6000%2C1400&w=1200&h=280","Z6TI_pbqstJ9-Tfc",{"x":48,"y":160,"zoom":49,"background":69},2173,{"dimensions":162,"alt":156,"copyright":30,"url":165,"id":158,"edit":166},{"width":163,"height":164},704,240,"everything-you-need-to-know-about-sustainable-packaging.html\u002F\u002Fimages.prismic.io\u002Fev-mercury\u002FZ6TI_pbqstJ9-Tfc_EVRI_LOCATION_03_2589.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&rect=0%2C947%2C6000%2C2045&w=704&h=240",{"x":48,"y":167,"zoom":49,"background":69},947,{"dimensions":169,"alt":156,"copyright":30,"url":172,"id":158,"edit":173},{"width":170,"height":171},343,160,"everything-you-need-to-know-about-sustainable-packaging.html\u002F\u002Fimages.prismic.io\u002Fev-mercury\u002FZ6TI_pbqstJ9-Tfc_EVRI_LOCATION_03_2589.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&rect=0%2C570%2C6000%2C2799&w=343&h=160",{"x":48,"y":174,"zoom":49,"background":69},570,"photo_block$3e52e853-383b-46a0-9a2c-3a02408fa1b2","photo_block",{"variation":25,"version":26,"items":178,"primary":180,"id":220,"slice_type":88,"slice_label":30},[179],{},{"CardImage":181,"CardAvatar":70,"CardTitle":187,"CardText":188,"ButtonText":30,"ButtonUrl":219,"IsEco":21},{"dimensions":182,"alt":183,"copyright":30,"url":184,"id":185,"edit":186},{"width":62,"height":63},"A father is measuring the sides of his parcel at home at his desk using measuring tape. His children are resting on the sofa behind him","everything-you-need-to-know-about-sustainable-packaging.html\u002F\u002Fimages.prismic.io\u002Fev-mercury\u002FZ6zc_pbqstJ9-inX_EVRI_LOCATION_05_7760.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&rect=0%2C8%2C8192%2C5448&w=1000&h=665","Z6zc_pbqstJ9-inX",{"x":48,"y":68,"zoom":49,"background":69},"1. Reuse cardboard boxes",[189,192,195,198,202,205,208,211,214],{"type":34,"text":190,"spans":191},"One of the best types of eco-friendly packaging is reused cardboard boxes. Whether you have spare cardboard boxes at home or in your stockroom, this is an environmentally friendly way to send items through our network.",[],{"type":34,"text":193,"spans":194},"You should always avoid buying new cardboard boxes, as these can contribute to deforestation, and sending items in reused cardboard boxes is much more sustainable. However, if you do need to use a new cardboard box to place your items in, ensure it’s from a sustainable source, and that it is made from certified paper such as Forest Stewardship Council (FSC). Otherwise, it can’t be classified as sustainable packaging.",[],{"type":34,"text":196,"spans":197},"These are the advantages of using old cardboard boxes and packaging when sending parcels:",[],{"type":199,"text":200,"spans":201},"list-item","Lighter cardboard reduces energy emissions – and takes less energy to transport, making it more sustainable. ",[],{"type":199,"text":203,"spans":204},"It’s more biodegradable than plastic and be easily recycled kerbside.",[],{"type":199,"text":206,"spans":207},"Affordability – cardboard is one of the best sustainable packaging options, but it’s also one of the cheapest.",[],{"type":199,"text":209,"spans":210},"Reusability – you can reuse cardboard boxes again and again, so long as they remain sturdy and protective.",[],{"type":199,"text":212,"spans":213},"Protection – you can use sturdy layers of cardboard as a protective shell to keep shipped items secure. ",[],{"type":34,"text":215,"spans":216},"Top tip: Before reusing a cardboard box to package your items, ensure there are no outdated labels or barcodes visible. These could be detected by our scanners and send your parcel to the wrong address.  ",[217],{"start":48,"end":218,"type":85},9,{"link_type":38},"card$d2db9009-7d96-4184-9c7a-f28a1332f63b",{"variation":25,"version":26,"items":222,"primary":224,"id":249,"slice_type":88,"slice_label":30},[223],{},{"CardImage":225,"CardAvatar":70,"CardTitle":231,"CardText":232,"ButtonText":30,"ButtonUrl":248,"IsEco":21},{"dimensions":226,"alt":227,"copyright":30,"url":228,"id":229,"edit":230},{"width":62,"height":63},"Customer sat at a desk placing their items into a box, ready to be packaged up for delivery.","everything-you-need-to-know-about-sustainable-packaging.html\u002F\u002Fimages.prismic.io\u002Fev-mercury\u002FZ6R5zpbqstJ9-STu_EVRI_LOCATION_05_8570.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&rect=0%2C8%2C8192%2C5448&w=1000&h=665","Z6R5zpbqstJ9-STu",{"x":48,"y":68,"zoom":49,"background":69},"2. Reused paper for padding",[233,236,239,242,245],{"type":34,"text":234,"spans":235},"One of the best sustainable packaging options is to use layers of paper when packaging your parcels. Just recycle old newspapers you’ve finished reading or any spare paper you have. Then, scrunch this paper and fill any noticeable gaps between your parcel box and the item you’re sending.",[],{"type":34,"text":237,"spans":238},"This eco-friendly packaging also encourages others to recycle when sending parcels through our network. ",[],{"type":34,"text":240,"spans":241},"Other advantages include:",[],{"type":199,"text":243,"spans":244},"Encouraging recycling - the person receiving your parcel can keep this newspaper and repeat this packaging process when they next mail an item. ",[],{"type":199,"text":246,"spans":247},"Affordability - reusing newspaper is an affordable option as well as a sustainable one.",[],{"link_type":38},"card$bae7d307-765f-4fb7-8a9f-67553a6b7535",{"variation":251,"version":26,"items":252,"primary":254,"id":270,"slice_type":88,"slice_label":30},"cardNoImageWithCta",[253],{},{"CardAvatar":70,"CardTitle":255,"CardText":256,"ButtonText":30,"ButtonUrl":269,"IsEco":21},"3.\tRecycled bubble wrap",[257,260,263,266],{"type":34,"text":258,"spans":259},"Reusing bubble wrap is a great way to recycle packaging while sending items through our network, and it also keeps items secure.  ",[],{"type":34,"text":261,"spans":262},"Bubble wrap isn’t sustainable, so to speak, but it is eco-friendly when you recycle it. If you already have bubble wrap stored away, we’d recommend recycling it when shipping items.",[],{"type":34,"text":264,"spans":265},"Covering fragile items with bubble wrap is a great way to reuse this packaging material, too, as you’ll be putting it to good use, instead of throwing it away.",[],{"type":34,"text":267,"spans":268},"Top tip: Bubble wrap is used for packaging items to protect them, thanks to the durable air bubbles. So, ensure the bubble wrap you’re reusing isn’t damaged before wrapping it around the items you’re sending.",[],{"link_type":38},"card$3b778057-c6c6-4c50-88b6-ac8ba0bc76f5",{"variation":25,"version":26,"items":272,"primary":274,"id":330,"slice_type":88,"slice_label":30},[273],{},{"CardImage":275,"CardAvatar":70,"CardTitle":281,"CardText":282,"ButtonText":318,"ButtonUrl":319,"IsEco":21},{"dimensions":276,"alt":277,"copyright":30,"url":278,"id":279,"edit":280},{"width":62,"height":63},"A customer is crouched on the floor of their apartment, holding recyclable packaging in one hand and items in another.","everything-you-need-to-know-about-sustainable-packaging.html\u002F\u002Fimages.prismic.io\u002Fev-mercury\u002FZ6XrQ5bqstJ9-WdM_EVRI_LOCATION_04_4977.jpg?auto=format%2Ccompress&rect=0%2C8%2C8192%2C5448&w=1000&h=665","Z6XrQ5bqstJ9-WdM",{"x":48,"y":68,"zoom":49,"background":69},"4. Use eco-friendly tape to wrap your items",[283,286,289,295],{"type":34,"text":284,"spans":285,"direction":86},"Typically, you’ll use traditional parcel tape to seal your items shut, ready to send. But a great, easy way to be more eco-conscious with your parcels is to use tape that’s renewable and easily compostable, rather than plastic tape. With some tape types, the person receiving your item can easily recycle the parcel, too.",[],{"type":34,"text":287,"spans":288,"direction":86},"Certain packing tapes are recyclable, such as standard or reinforced gummed paper tape. If they’re not reusing it, they can place the box straight in the recycling bin, without having to remove the tape first.  ",[],{"type":34,"text":290,"spans":291,"direction":86},"There you have it; now that you know our best sustainable packaging options, you can use more eco-friendly materials to send parcels through our network.",[292],{"start":293,"end":294,"type":85},67,68,{"type":34,"text":296,"spans":297,"direction":86}," For more packaging advice, check out the Evri blog, and read through our guides about topics like how to regift a present and how to package books.",[298,304,305,308,312,317],{"start":299,"end":300,"type":79,"data":301},42,51,{"link_type":81,"url":302,"target":303},"everything-you-need-to-know-about-sustainable-packaging.html\u002F\u002Fwww.evri.com\u002Fnews","_blank",{"start":299,"end":300,"type":85},{"start":306,"end":307,"type":85},98,122,{"start":309,"end":307,"type":79,"data":310},99,{"link_type":81,"url":311,"target":303},"everything-you-need-to-know-about-sustainable-packaging.html\u002F\u002Fwww.evri.com\u002Fguides\u002Fa-guide-to-re-gifting-the-right-way",{"start":313,"end":314,"type":79,"data":315},127,147,{"link_type":81,"url":316,"target":303},"everything-you-need-to-know-about-sustainable-packaging.html\u002F\u002Fwww.evri.com\u002Fguides\u002Fhow-to-package-books",{"start":313,"end":314,"type":85},"Send a parcel with Evri",{"id":320,"type":321,"tags":322,"lang":16,"slug":324,"first_publication_date":325,"last_publication_date":326,"uid":327,"url":328,"link_type":19,"key":329,"isBroken":21},"YiX9JBIAACsAFthQ","landing-page",[323],"Send a Parcel","why-send-a-parcel-with-evri","2022-03-07T12:41:12+0000","2026-07-09T13:59:25+0000","send","\u002Fsend","194d0b92-aa78-41c1-a59c-31a4e68c7ed4","card$84edbbfc-cca4-440f-a503-784bbbc1a225",[24,55,89,109,148,177,221,250,271],["Reactive",333],{"$sglobal-feature-switches":334,"$sclients":400,"$sglobal-basket-c